# r1113 client batch for the -17 jar (phase 10): throwaway client (eval_client.py setup, the -17 PG jar
# jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar copied into GAME/mods only, never the instance's mods/),
# singleplayer copy of the pwg17 scratch world (sp_world.py) after pwg17.qb has run (its SQ-PWG-SHOW17 step leaves lit
# string lights, a plating wall and a lit ceiling at X 1100 to 1123, Z 2010 to 2084). Before: client in that world,
# op (cheats on), chat closed, no screen open, window 854x480.
# Covers what chat commands, keys and screenshots can do for CQ-PWG-22, -24, -26, -27, -28 and -29. Not possible here,
# left as `look` steps for the owner: right-clicks (opening the design table and the editor, attaching to tiles, cords,
# hand boost), mouse hover (tooltips), and JEI lookups (typing into JEI's search box needs a click on it; the box
# position depends on the GUI scale, so it is not scripted). No probe commands: the client game dir has no zz_ probes.
# Run: qrun.py client GAME tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113/cq_pwg17.qb perf/runs/r1113/cq_pwg17
pace 2

